<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dīa</span></b> , ae, f., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῖα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The old name of the island of</i> Naxos, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				690</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 174</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city in the</i> Chersonesus Taurica, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				26, § 86</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An island near Crete</i>, now <i>Standia</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 4, 12, 20, §
			61</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A woman's name</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The mother of Mercury</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 22, 56</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The wife of Ixion, and mother of Pirithous</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg.
				F. 155</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
